"""Scientific TASK for joining compatible saved experimental components."""

COMPILED_ASSAY_TASK = """Evaluate what the selected experimental measurements establish about the studied molecule's measured activity and the functional assertion under investigation. Identify the actual molecule, construct, preparation, experimental system, endpoint, conditions and intended variable. Use source-supported context already available or examine the relevant source when needed. A function may emerge from the investigation; an initial candidate annotation is not required.

Select the saved numerical components that answer the assigned question. Establish each component's physical meaning, units, denominator and relationship to the particular assay. Matching names, units or publication do not establish applicability. Preserve the distinction between the directly measured endpoint and the asserted molecular function, including unresolved reporter-to-product relationships.

Determine which corrections have already been applied. Distinguish sample-minus-blank rate from gross signal, separately measured contamination from background already removed, instrument recovery from an enzyme-spike response, and total-molecule amount from active-site amount. Do not repeat subtraction, calibration or normalization already incorporated in a measurement. Preserve incompatible measurements as useful evidence while leaving the unsupported combined result unavailable.

Examine comparability outside the intended change and isolation of the measured effect separately. A condition-control response must address the relevant nuisance difference while excluding the variable deliberately tested. Establish whether compared molecules replace one another or coexist. Preserve additional changes, mixed contributors and alternative explanations rather than treating a control label as proof of isolation.

Preserve the underlying measurement owners and shared inputs across components. A calculated recovery ratio depends on its measured and nominal standards; a net optical rate can share background, calibration or path-length inputs with other results. Do not treat derived quantities as independent because they appear in different sections. Retain reported uncertainty and replication meanings; select covariance and a sampling model only when supported.

Nominate the applicable saved operands, experimental relationships and correction stages. Deterministic functions perform validation, unit conversion and arithmetic. Retain usable partial results when a relationship, measurement or required implementation is missing, and distinguish those reasons. Return only the requested numerical sections and their necessary qualifications. Do not invent missing controls, a universal quality grade, function probability, target-transfer weight or cross-assay total.

Assess uncertainty for the particular numerical result requested. Activity per molecular amount can have supported uncertainty even when additional contamination or condition corrections are unknown. Use the joint uncertainty of the actual operands, retaining shared measurements and signed covariance. Keep uncertainty propagated from those operands separate from additional residual variability. Do not invent missing corrections, assume missing covariance is zero, or present a partial result’s uncertainty as the uncertainty of a fully corrected activity."""

OPERATION_DESCRIPTION = "Compile compatible already received source-component cells into the studied assay's numerical measurement, calibration, comparability, attribution, normalization and uncertainty sections. Select source-supported experimental meanings and correction stages; do not enter scientific values. Preserve shared measurements and unknown covariance. Apply the existing source-activity correction only to its appropriate endpoint and units, once. Return exact requested saved numerical components, not a universal reliability grade, target-transfer weight or annotation credit."
